-- A terminal cell holds two dots, one above the other, so the picture below is 96 across
-- and 60 down in real colour.

please open a canvas 96 across and 60 down

please remember sky is the colour called "sky" or 0
please remember sun is the colour called "lamp" or 0
please remember near is the colour called "moss" or 0
please remember far is the colour called "dark green" or 0

please clear the canvas to sky

-- The sun, and the light around it.
please draw a circle at the point 74 and 14 of size 12 in the colour with red 240 green 200 blue 120
please draw a circle at the point 74 and 14 of size 8 in sun

-- Hills, the far one first so the near one sits in front of it.
please repeat for every x from 0 to 95:
    remember height is 40 plus the rounded version of 6 times the sine of x divided by 9
    draw a line from the point x and height to the point x and 59 in far
thank you for repeating

please repeat for every x from 0 to 95:
    remember height is 48 plus the rounded version of 5 times the sine of x divided by 5
    draw a line from the point x and height to the point x and 59 in near
thank you for repeating

